## Summary

I shipped a complete, production-grade native SwiftUI **`SavedViewMenu`** surface at parity with the web source `components/data-display/SavedViewMenu.tsx`, in the mandated `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/` location (12 files, ~2,073 Swift LOC), following the repo's established sibling architecture.

**What's implemented (full parity + P4 leaf contract):** trigger button (collapses to active view name), popover row list with per-row pull-down actions (apply / set-default / pin / rename / delete), applied badge with clear, save/rename/manage sheets, delete `confirmationDialog`, once-only default auto-apply (web mount effect), and every required state — loading / empty / error / ready plus live/stale/offline freshness (chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh). Binds through `SavedViewMenuModel` (P1/S8), localizes via the P1/S10 facade (38 keys, no English literals), emits `view.opened` (P1/S11), and has VoiceOver labels + an accessibility announcer throughout.

